  "final_message": "The key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nHere's the path. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`. That function builds the key with `_format_key(kind, ident)`, which returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`, and `config.py` sets `AUDIT_PREFIX` to `\"AUD\"`.\n\nThe key line in `audit.py` showed up redacted when I first read the file, so I checked the raw bytes to confirm it really calls `_format_key`. I also ran `write_audit('order', '7781')` directly, and it returned `{'AUD-ORDER-7781': True}`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` looks similar but uses the `MET` prefix and writes to a metrics dict, not the audit log. `decoy_cache.py` doesn't touch the audit log either.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
